<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Hardened Runtime.

  Deliberately minimal. The privileged write path spawns /usr/libexec/authopen,
  passes a file descriptor back over a UNIX domain socket with SCM_RIGHTS, and
  then writes to that descriptor. None of that is restricted by the Hardened
  Runtime, so none of it needs a positive entitlement.

  What it does need is for the App Sandbox to stay off, which is what this file
  records. See the pull request for the list of entitlements that were
  considered and deliberately left out.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Required to stay false.

	  The App Sandbox forbids executing setuid helpers, and a sandboxed process
	  passes its sandbox on to anything it spawns, so turning this on would
	  break the authopen handshake outright rather than degrade it. Tauri does
	  not enable the sandbox by default; this states the dependency explicitly
	  so that it is a deliberate decision to change rather than an accident.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
